From 4bc67e1902841a4c66376538ce07ac8f734ca366 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:59:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: ilitek-ili9881c: Add Innolux AFJ101-BA2131 support

Add support for the Innolux AFJ101-BA2131, the 10.1" 800x1280 4-lane
MIPI-DSI panel Xunlong ships as the "Orange Pi 10.1 inch MIPI LCD" for
the Orange Pi 5 family. Its init sequence (ILI9881C page select
FF 98 81 xx) shows it uses an ILI9881C controller, so add it to the
existing driver rather than as a new one.

The init sequence (pages 3, 4 and 1), the display mode, the physical
size and the DSI mode flags come from the Orange Pi BSP driver
drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-innolux-afj101-ba2131.c in
https://github.com/orangepi-xunlong/linux-orangepi, branch
orange-pi-6.1-rk35xx (GPL-2.0+). The trailing page 0 commands of the
vendor table (sleep out, display on, tear on) are left out because the
driver sends them itself.

The vendor driver toggles an "enable" GPIO before reset; on the boards
it is the LCD power enable, which is described here as the panel's
power-supply regulator.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
